    "title": "Momentum regime — observed slippage above 2σ",
    "body": "## Observation\n\nDuring the April 14–16 high-volatility window, strategy **MOM-v3** showed consistent bid-ask slippage above the 2σ threshold on ES futures.\n\nThe effect was most pronounced in the 09:30–10:00 window. Slippage peaked at 3.1σ on April 15 at 09:47 ET.\n\n## Hypothesis\n\nThe fill-delay budget in the execution profile may be underestimating intraday opening-auction latency. Recommend adjusting `fill_delay_budget_ms` from 120ms to 160ms for the opening 30-minute window and re-running the backtest.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Link to slippage analysis artifact once RW experiment is complete.\n- Cross-reference against the momentum regime pattern in institutional memory.",
